{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "261750785",
    "title": "Development Standards",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/261750785",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 2,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "General day-to-day coding conventions for the Zimmermann PWA Kit. For the pattern used to override a base Salesforce component vs. build a new Zimmermann-specific one, see [Component Override Strategy](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/261881857).\n\nNaming conventions\n------------------\n\n| What | Convention | Example |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| New Zimmermann files and folders | `camelCase` | `backInStockButton/`, `useWishlist.ts` |\n| Overrides of Salesforce base files | Keep upstream kebab-case exactly | `product-tile/index.tsx` |\n| Component named export | Matches folder name | `BackInStockButton` exported from `backInStockButton/` |\n| Component props type | Component name + `Props` | `BackInStockButtonProps` |\n| Hook files | `.ts` (not `.tsx`) | `useWishlist.ts` |\n| Hook export | Matches filename | `useWishlist` |\n| Callback props | `onEventName` | `onAddToCart`, `onClose` |\n| Identifiers and copy | Australian spelling | `colour`, `centre`, `organisation` |\n| Override files | Keep upstream Salesforce spelling verbatim | — |\n\nTypeScript only inside `overrides/`. No `.js` or `.jsx` files. Run `npx tsc --noEmit` before finishing any task that touches `overrides/`.\n\nNo `any` without an inline comment explaining why a narrower type is impossible.\n\nPrefer `type` over `interface` for component props and shared shapes.\n\nDesign tokens\n-------------\n\nDesign tokens (colours, typography, spacing) live in `overrides/app/theme/foundation/` — **frozen (Tier 1)**, owned by the UI Designer. Do not modify except to sync with Figma; ask the UI Designer if a needed colour/font isn't in the token set.\n\nDefaulttsx// ✅ correct — uses the token\n<Text color=\"brand.primary\" fontSize=\"md\">…</Text>\n// ❌ wrong — hardcoded value\n<Text color=\"#1a1a1a\" fontSize=\"16px\">…</Text>\n\nPer-component theme overrides (button variant, link styles, etc.) live in `overrides/app/theme/components/` — Tier 2 (protected), owned by the UI Designer.\n\nCommon shared components\n------------------------\n\n| Component | Path | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Header | `overrides/app/components/header/` | Tier 2 — coordinate with both squads before touching |\n| Page container | `overrides/app/components/pageContainer/` | Wraps page-level layout |\n| App config | `overrides/app/components/_app-config/` | Tier 2 |\n| Button | `overrides/app/components/button/` | Zimmermann button override |\n\nFor icons, use `@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/components/icons`. If a required icon is missing, get it from Figma or ask the UI Designer — do not substitute a visually different one.\n\nStyling\n-------\n\n1. Chakra UI props first.\n2. `.scss` file alongside the component only when Chakra props cannot achieve the required result.\n\nNever hardcode hex colours, pixel spacing values, or raw font sizes in component props.\n\nStorybook\n---------\n\nEvery component exported from `overrides/app/components/` or `overrides/app/pages/` must have a `.stories.tsx` file.\n\n| Category | What goes here |\n| --- | --- |\n| `Foundation/` | Design token visualisations |\n| `Elements/` | Generic building blocks (Button, Input, Badge) |\n| `Commerce/` | Commerce-specific components (ProductTile, OrderSummary) |\n| `Layout/` | Global shell (Header, Footer, DrawerMenu) |\n| `Forms/` | Form assemblies (AddressForm, CheckoutContactForm) |\n| `Pages/` | Full page assemblies (PDP, PLP, Cart) |\n\nEvery story file needs a `Default` named export. Add named exports for meaningful states (`Loading`, `OutOfStock`) — not for every prop combination.\n\nTesting\n-------\n\n| Layer | Tool | When |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Unit | Vitest | Data mapping, transforms, hook logic in isolation |\n| Component interaction | Storybook `play` | User interactions (clicks, form fills, focus) |\n| E2E | Playwright | Full user journeys across pages |\n\nVitest tests co-locate with source as `*.test.ts`.\n\nBefore opening a PR\n-------------------\n\nDefaultbashnpx tsc --noEmit # TypeScript must be clean\nnpm run lint # lint must pass\nnpm run test # unit tests must pass\n\nClaude Code's `/code-quality` skill runs a pre-PR audit of changed files; `/pr-checklist` generates a structured PR description.\n\nFile protection tiers\n---------------------\n\nNot all files are equally safe to edit.\n\n| Tier | What | Rule |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Tier 1 — Frozen** | Design tokens, shared commerce hooks, SSR/config, CI/CD | Stop. Get owner approval before any change. |\n| **Tier 2 — Protected** | Global shell, shared product components, translations, shared hooks | PR requires a second reviewer. Notify the owner. |\n| **Unclassified** | A squad's own feature components and pages | Normal feature-branch workflow. |\n\nFull lists live in the repo's `.claude/rules/frozenFiles.md` and `.claude/rules/protectedFiles.md`.",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "1f680",
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

