    "content": {
      "value": "This page covers the DOM-crawl-era findings (67 pages, before we had Magento API access). For the real Page Builder structure behind five representative pages — pulled straight from Magento and parsed as an actual tree, not inferred from rendered HTML — see **[5.9.3a — Magento Component Patterns & Mapping](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/465371162)**. That page is now the more authoritative source for anything it covers; this page still holds everything it doesn't (the full Zimmerse gap analysis, the spikes, the Jira story review).\n\nThe constraint we're building around\n------------------------------------\n\nThe SFCC PWA's existing components live under `overrides/app/components/` and extend base Salesforce Retail React App components — they weren't built to stand alone, and we can't reuse them for pure-Contentful pages. So everything for this work lives in two new folders:\n\n* `overrides/app/components/contentful/components/` — the atoms/molecules/organisms for individual content blocks\n* `overrides/app/components/contentful/experiences/` — the subset of those registered to Contentful Studio Experiences via `@cf-register` and `npm run generate:contentful` (see the `contentful-register-component` skill for how that registration actually works)\n\nBoth folders exist already but are empty. There was an earlier \"Hardi-era\" attempt at `experiences/*.tsx` that got removed as unused scaffolding, so there's nothing to build on there — we're starting clean.\n\n**One real exception found (2026-09-02):** the footer's newsletter signup component, `ZimmSubscribeSection` (`overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmSubscribeSection/`), was already extracted from the footer specifically so it could be placed on any page, not just the global footer — its own doc comment says so. It has no SFCC/commerce-sdk-react hook dependency today (the real Omneo submission is still pending HPC-036; right now it's a placeholder state machine), and it's a clean container/presentational split already. This is the one component we don't need to build twice for the Contentful side — see 5.9.2 for how it plugs in.\n\nSharing tokens, not components\n------------------------------\n\nWe're not trying to reuse the SFCC-side components, but we do want to reuse the design system underneath them. New components reach for Chakra props plus `var(--zimm-*)` tokens and `textStyle`, exactly per `overrideStyling.md`, with no dependency on any SFCC hook. That keeps one design language across commerce and content pages while the actual component code stays fully independent.\n\nThree things we need to spike before building too much more\n-----------------------------------------------------------\n\n**1. Contentful's own grid vs. building our own.** Contentful Experiences ships its own layout primitives on the canvas — sections, containers, columns — that editors can use to arrange components without us building anything. Before we commit to custom Zimmermann grid components wired into `gridSystem.ts`/`.zimm-grid`, we should try building a page with Contentful's default layout blocks and see how far that actually gets us.\n\n**2. How well Chakra plays with Contentful Experiences.** We're building these components on Chakra and our existing token set, and Contentful's Experience Builder has its own idea of how a component exposes editable properties and responsive behaviour on the canvas. We haven't tried connecting the two yet — worth building one or two simple components all the way through (Chakra-styled, `@cf-register`'d, bound to real content, editable in Studio) before we've built more than a couple and discover friction the hard way.\n\n**3. Conditional field visibility in the entry editor.** Now that `link.js` is getting a `variant` field (Primary/Secondary) that only makes sense when `style` is set to Button, we've got our first real case of needing to show or hide a field based on another field's value — something Contentful's default entry editor can't do out of the box. This needs a custom Contentful app (a field editor or entry-sidebar extension) to actually pull off. Worth its own spike, since we'll hit this exact need again as the model set grows (the CTA case today, more field-in-service-of-another-field decisions later).\n\nAll three should probably become their own tickets once we're ready to size them — flagging them here so they don't get lost in the meantime.\n\nWhat we actually found on the live site (67 pages reviewed, 2026-09-02)\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nEvery component below links to at least one real page we saw it on — click through rather than take the description on faith. The full page-by-page breakdown, with per-page model/component counts kept in sync with this page's taxonomy, lives on [5.9.1a — Full Page Inventory](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/465633295).\n\n### Solid — build these as scoped\n\n| Component | Backing model | Jira story | See it live |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Multi-image gallery/grid | `image` (array) | SFCC-546 | [runway-fall-rtw-2026](https://www.zimmermann.com/runway-fall-rtw-2026) (a 52-look gallery), [details-cruise-rtw-2027](https://www.zimmermann.com/details-cruise-rtw-2027) |\n| Rich text / editorial copy | Rich Text | SFCC-543 | [sustainability-approach](https://www.zimmermann.com/sustainability-approach), [our-story](https://www.zimmermann.com/our-story) |\n| Section heading | Simple Text | SFCC-540 | [collections](https://www.zimmermann.com/collections), [cruise-rtw-2027](https://www.zimmermann.com/cruise-rtw-2027) |\n| Hero image (full-bleed, with or without overlay/CTA) | Image & Text | SFCC-534 / SFCC-541 | [fall-rtw-2026](https://www.zimmermann.com/fall-rtw-2026), [boutique/paris](https://www.zimmermann.com/boutique/paris) |\n| Inline image + caption | `image` | SFCC-544 / SFCC-545 | [z-x-atlasharmonic](https://www.zimmermann.com/z-x-atlasharmonic), [janet-laurence](https://www.zimmermann.com/janet-laurence) |\n| Article card + card grid (hub pages) | Image & Text | SFCC-537 / SFCC-539 | [z-art](https://www.zimmermann.com/z-art), [sustainability](https://www.zimmermann.com/sustainability) |\n| Back/Next pagination nav | 2× `link` — **confirmed editor-authored**, not derived (see [5.9.3a](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/465371162)) | SFCC-548 | [jedda-daisy-culley](https://www.zimmermann.com/jedda-daisy-culley), [remy-faint-paris](https://www.zimmermann.com/remy-faint-paris) |\n| Accordion / FAQ group | Accordion/FAQ Item | *(not yet a Jira story — see 5.9.2)* | [faq](https://www.zimmermann.com/faq) (5 groups), [shipping](https://www.zimmermann.com/shipping) (12 groups) |\n| Newsletter signup | Reuses `ZimmSubscribeSection` directly — see above, no new component | *(existing footer component)* | `subscribe-newsletter` |\n\n### New — we saw these again and again, but nothing in Jira covers them\n\n| Component | Backing model | See it live | Why it matters |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Shoppable product caption / product-grid carousel** | Thin product/SKU reference — the client has confirmed an SFCC app is already installed capable of loading products/categories, which de-risks this considerably (see 5.9.2) | [fall-rtw-2026-campaign](https://www.zimmermann.com/fall-rtw-2026-campaign), [accessories-fall-rtw-2026](https://www.zimmermann.com/accessories-fall-rtw-2026), [goldentime-collection](https://www.zimmermann.com/goldentime-collection) | The single most consistent pattern with zero Jira coverage — 97 of 299 pages use it once you count all three of its Magento widget names (see 5.9.3a) |\n| **Instagram feed embed** | None — a live third-party embed, title + link only | [subscribe-newsletter](https://www.zimmermann.com/subscribe-newsletter) and 6 other pages, confirmed via Magento's `zfeed` content-type (`Tryzens\\ZFeed\\Block\\Widget\\ZFeed`, \"FOLLOW US ON INSTAGRAM\") — see [5.9.3a](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/465371162) | Needs Didomi consent gating like any other third-party script per AGENTS.md; missed by the original DOM-crawl sample, only turned up once we analysed all 299 pages |\n| Breadcrumb navigation | Likely derived from page hierarchy — still an open question, unlike Back/Next Nav this one wasn't settled by the real Magento data | [making-of-fall-26](https://www.zimmermann.com/making-of-fall-26), [contactus](https://www.zimmermann.com/contactus) | Distinct from SFCC-548's back/next pattern |\n| Card grid with \"Read more/less\" expand toggle | Image & Text | [collections](https://www.zimmermann.com/collections), [z-projects](https://www.zimmermann.com/z-projects) | Real interactive behaviour beyond a static card |\n| Pull-quote / blockquote block | Pull Quote | [remy-faint-paris](https://www.zimmermann.com/remy-faint-paris), [our-story](https://www.zimmermann.com/our-story) | Visually distinct from generic rich text — still a low sample size |\n| Editorial → commerce CTA button | `link` (extended) | [the-zimmermann-sound-of-summer](https://www.zimmermann.com/the-zimmermann-sound-of-summer) | Cross-sells from editorial content straight into a PLP |\n| External-brand CTA link | `link` (extended) | [z-x-atlas-harmonic](https://www.zimmermann.com/z-x-atlas-harmonic) (links out to atlasharmonic.com) | Just the extended `link` primitive with different styling |\n| Size / measurement table | Table | [size-chart](https://www.zimmermann.com/size-chart) | Five genuine tables |\n| Icon grid + regional accordion | Image & Text + Accordion/FAQ Item | [contactus](https://www.zimmermann.com/contactus) | May be fully composable from things we're already building, rather than needing its own component |\n| Nav group (Quick Links / Help sidebar) | `navGroup` (pending PR) | [accessibility](https://www.zimmermann.com/accessibility), [contactus](https://www.zimmermann.com/contactus) | Reuses the generalised nav group once that PR merges |\n\nThe Document Flip-book Gallery we'd flagged earlier turned out not to need its own component — it's just the Multi-Image Gallery, since [sustainability-report-24](https://www.zimmermann.com/sustainability-report-24) is really just images embedded on a page.\n\n### Existing Jira stories worth a second look\n\n| Story | What we found |\n| --- | --- |\n| **SFCC-547 (Vimeo embed)** | Not one confirmed video embed across all 24 Zimmerse pages we looked at, and none in the 5 real pages pulled for 5.9.3a either — though Magento's `collections-tile` does have unpopulated video fields (`video_ratio`/`video_autoplay`), so the capability exists in the CMS even if nothing live uses it yet |\n| **SFCC-538 (Category/tag label)** | No tag or pill UI anywhere in the sample — categorical info reads as plain text in headings and captions |\n| **SFCC-542 (the date half)** | The byline half holds up — [jedda-daisy-culley](https://www.zimmermann.com/jedda-daisy-culley) and two other Z.Gallery pages show it — but we never once saw a publish date on any of the 24 pages. Now that Date is a real field on Image & Text (see 5.9.2), this is really just a question of whether SFCC-532's article model actually needs it populated |\n| **SFCC-549 (Related articles rail)** | Never saw a multi-card rail — the site consistently uses a single Back/Next link (SFCC-548) instead |\n| **SFCC-536 (Wordmark/logo)** | Only ever appears in the global header, never as something an editor places inside the article body — might not need to be a placeable CMS component at all |\n\nWorth being upfront that these are findings from a sample, not a verdict — before touching any of these five stories, it's worth checking with the client or design team in case there's editorial direction coming that our sample just didn't happen to catch.\n\nFigma coverage\n--------------\n\n[Zimmermann Designs — Zimmerse](https://www.figma.com/design/QQ427wHWEUjsjP7H8v48Rs/Zimmermann_Designs?node-id=3401-40749) only covers Zimmerse, and even there it's known to be incomplete. The other five page types have no design coverage at all, so we're deriving their component needs from what's actually live on the site rather than from a spec — which is exactly what the table above is doing.\n\nStill open\n----------\n\n* All three spikes above — none started yet\n* Whether Breadcrumb is genuinely derived-not-authored — Back/Next Nav turned out not to be an exception, this one's still unconfirmed\n* Which of the components above need full Contentful Studio Experience registration versus just living inside a fixed field structure\n* Governance: neither `overrides/app/components/contentful/**` folder is in CODEOWNERS or `protectedFiles.md` yet\n* Whether to draft the actual Jira story updates and additions this gap analysis points to — not started yet, waiting on direction",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "1f9e9",
    "page_width": "full-width"
  }
}"}

